      "text": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the same person across all three references. Use <Picture 1> for her dark wavy hair and full bangs, <Picture 2> for her facial features and forearm tattoo, and <Picture 3> for her three-quarter facial profile.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] Create a single candid beach portrait of <Subject 1> from behind, with bare shoulders and an opaque towel wrapped around her.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - retain her facial identity, hairstyle, and visible tattoo placement.\n\ndetailed_description:\nA medium-quality amateur phone photo taken from a few steps away in late-afternoon light, with slightly bright sand and soft detail in the distance.\n\n[Shot 1] <Subject 1> sits on a low driftwood log facing the ocean, wrapped in an opaque navy towel that covers her chest and lap. Both feet rest in the sand. Her tattooed forearm rests along the log beside her, and her free hand holds the folded towel in place. Turn her head back just enough to show her three-quarter profile and a relaxed, closed-mouth smile. Photograph her from behind and slightly to one side, framing her from head to knees with the surf beyond her. Hold the result as a single still photograph.\n\noverall_soundscape: N/A\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A"
